// Selection.select is the SELECT counterpart to Overlay.highlight's hover, and shares its Ui tier for the same
// reason: it paints chrome on the target and starts scroll tracking, it does not write the app. The badge it
// raises opens no editing panel (DevToolsOverlay_SelectHandle passes fromUserPick=false); the quick-edit surface it
// offers is still gated independently by the process write posture. Gating selection itself at Mutation would
// make the ordinary "click a tree row" gesture demand editing consent, which no in-process surface does.
//
// Its result is SelectionSelectResult, not the bare SelectionResult Selection.poll returns: it has to say
// whether the selection actually moved (see the type's own note), which a poll never has to answer.
WINAPP_DEVTOOLS_PROTOCOL_METHOD(SelectionSelect,           L"Selection.select",              L"Selection",  DevToolsAccess::Ui,       DevToolsVisibility::Public, OwnerHandleParams,       SelectionSelectResult)
